UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105033222662?origin=resultslist
AB  - This paper introduces an advanced architectural framework integrating Virtual Reality, Artificial Intelligence, and sophisticated 3D reconstruction techniques. The architecture employs photogrammetry and terrestrial laser scanning to generate highly detailed and realistic virtual environments, providing seamless interaction through natural language commands. Central to the system is a conversational AI assistant powered by a locally hosted Large Language Model (LLM), enhanced by a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture, which ensures precise and contextually coherent responses. As a practical demonstration, the architecture is applied to digitally explore three historically significant rock churches in Matera, Italy. These churches feature intricate architectural and morphological characteristics such as steep terrain, narrow entrances, and uneven surfaces, which are meticulously reconstructed using Unreal Engine to create immersive, high-fidelity virtual representations. The system infrastructure is local, ensuring minimal latency and robust data privacy. The conversational AI component was rigorously evaluated through heritage-specific queries using RAG Assessment (RAGAS) metrics, including Context Precision, Entity Recall, and Faithfulness. The results confirm the system's robust performance and effectiveness, highlighting its capability to accurately convey detailed architectural and cultural knowledge. This approach demonstrates the considerable potential of integrating conversational AI and eXtended Reality technologies in detailed virtual explorations of complex heritage sites. © 2025 IEEE.
