AB  - This paper reports on the development of a new learning platform using Augmented Reality (AR) Technology) that leverages real-time image processing, interactive 3D visualization, chatbot dialogues, and "Vision"language models (VLLMs) to improve the user experience and learning outcomes. We developed the user interface for mobile AL learning using Unity and Vuforia to scan flashcards and textbook images, enabling learners to immerse and engage with the materials. The application retrieves and renders high fidelity 3D models of animals, alongside lifelike animations and spatial audio. To improve the interactive voice and text interfaces of learning systems, we integrated a domain-specific query processing chatbot; thus, learners have instant access to voice and text interactions. In addition, the retrieval of relevant text and images using VLLM enables the automatic searching for and displaying of view-rich visuals to aid exploration of the information. The modules offered include endangered and extinct species, various aquatic animals, and their spatial habitats, including gamification for better retention. User testing in real-world settings documented improved access, user engagement, and retention of knowledge. The research provides a real-world solution for learners using AR technology, serving as a flexible, intelligent, and interactive learning platform and a conversational interface. © 2025 IEEE.
