AB  - Dietary sub-health and diet-related chronic diseases are becoming increasingly prevalent worldwide, while professional nutritionist resources are extremely scarce. Meanwhile, existing AI-based smart glasses mainly focus on general functions such as information display, translation, and navigation, with no dedicated research or applications targeting dietary health management. To address this global challenge, we introduce AIRhealth, the first universal AR glasses framework for all human beings that unifies object detection, large language models, and data visualization into a single system. AIRhealth enables dish recognition, nutrient analysis, personalized recommendation, and visualized dietary health management. It integrates a camera, AR optical waveguide lenses, bone conduction speakers, multimodal large language models, and IoT-based edge-cloud collaboration. By applying knowledge distillation and LoRA fine-tuning to the Qwen2.5-VL 7B model, AIRhealth achieves professional-level dietary health reasoning with real-time AR interaction. Experimental results show that AIRhealth achieves excellent performance in dish recognition accuracy (classification accuracy of 70.17%), gesture interaction detection (gesture detection accuracy of 90.42%), and overall system performance (dataset overall score of 73.10%), with an Fl-score of 64.51%, providing a foundational framework for future personalized dietary health management worldwide. © 2025 IEEE.
