AB  - We propose the use of a Generative Adversarial Network (GAN) with depth images to generate shadows for virtual objects in mixed reality environments. This approach improves the accuracy of shadow generation process by aligning shadows with non-planar geometries. While traditional methods require detailed lighting and geometry data, recent research has emerged that generates shadows by learning from the image itself, even when such conditions are not fully known. However, these studies are limited to projecting shadows only onto the ground: a planar geometry. Our dataset used for training the GAN, includes depth images allows natural shadow generation in complex environments. © 2025 by SCITEPRESS - Science and Technology Publications, Lda.
