AB  - In this study, we present PolyLinguAR, an innovative learning experience platform that leverages web Augmented Reality (WebAR) and conversational AI to create an immersive, multilingual educational experience. PolyLinguAR features a life-sized AI avatar teacher that appears in the user’s real environment via a mobile web browser with no specialized hardware or apps required. The avatar delivers interactive lessons in multiple languages with real-time lip-synchronized speech and facial animations, providing visual pronunciation cues to learners. The system integrates speech-to-text (STT) to listen to learners’ spoken input and a Large Language Model (LLM) to generate contextually appropriate responses, which are then spoken by the avatar using text-to-speech (TTS) synthesis. The current initial prototype of PolyLinguAR focuses on a multilingual learning experience and demonstrates promising results which is real-time lip-sync across languages, responsive speech-based interactions, and positive learner engagement. By uniting WebAR and AI technologies, PolyLinguAR showcases a novel approach to learning experience, one that is widely accessible, highly engaging, and geared towards building linguistic proficiency. ©2025 IEEE.
