AB  - This paper presents an emotion-soothing system that integrates Virtual Reality (VR) with Artificial Intelligence (AI), emphasizing the use of large language models (LLMs) and multimodal interaction technologies. Central to the system is a virtual human developed in Unreal Engine 5 (UE5), which provides emotional support through rich, context-aware dialogue powered by ChatGPT. As the system's cognitive core, ChatGPT enables real-time, personalized conversations that mimic the behavior of a psychological counselor. To complement verbal interaction, the system incorporates multimodal components - including speech input, facial expression tracking, and gesture recognition - to enhance emotional sensitivity and user engagement. Controlled experiments evaluating anxiety reduction, physiological stress relief, and interaction satisfaction demonstrate that the combined use of LLMs and multimodal cues significantly improves emotional regulation outcomesTo evaluate the effectiveness of the system in emotion regulation, a set of controlled experiments was conducted. Participants' anxiety levels, physiological stress responses, and interaction satisfaction were quantitatively assessed. The experimental results demonstrate that the system significantly alleviates negative emotions and physiological stress while enhancing user engagement and overall satisfaction. © 2025 IEEE.
