AB  - Sri Lanka possesses a rich cultural heritage spanning more than two millennia. However, access to accurate, engaging, and context-aware historical knowledge remains limited for many learners and visitors. Conventional heritage interpretation methods such as guidebooks, static displays, and generic digital content often fail to provide spatial accuracy, temporal relevance, or personalized engagement. To address these limitations, this paper presents an Artificial Intelligence (AI) powered Virtual Reality (VR) platform for interactive learning and immersive exploration of historical events. The core contribution of this work is a tightly integrated architecture that combines geo-temporal personalization using GPS based location detection and era-based temporal filtering, a hybrid conversational AI system combining Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) with LoRA fine tuning of the Mistral-7B language model on a $\mathbf{2, 0 4 6}$ event Sri Lankan heritage dataset a spatially synchronized dual era VR environment enabling seamless transitions between modern and historical scenes, and an emotionally intelligent character framework that synchronizes AI-generated speech with procedurally generated gestures (Language of Motion, SMPL-X). Experimental evaluation demonstrates that the proposed hybrid RAG and LoRA system outperforms all baseline configurations, achieving a BERTScore of 0.924 and cultural accuracy of 88.5 %, while the K-Means clustering module attains a silhouette score of $\mathbf{0. 5 7 1 9}$. The platform is optimized for deployment on mid-range mobile VR hardware through multi-resolution asset streaming, level of detail management, and additive scene loading. Results confirm the feasibility of delivering personalized, immersive, and scalable cultural heritage experiences on mobile platforms © 2026 IEEE.
