AB  - Generative AI (GenAI) has made creating digital content easier than ever. But for kids, most of these tools still trap them behind a screen, missing out on the joy of hands-on play. We built Creatura Era, an arcade-style game that mixes GenAI, Augmented Reality (AR), and physical cards to let kids (aged 7–12) truly create together. It works in three simple steps: Create, Craft, and Play. Kids draw their own characters on the machine and describe them. Then, our system brings these drawings to life as 3D characters, prints them onto physical cards, and lets kids battle with them in AR. We tackled some big challenges along the way, like keeping content safe, handling wait times, and making sure kids feel like *they* made the art, not just the computer. Our results show that when designed right, GenAI can be a partner that boosts a child’s imagination, turning them from passive watchers into active creators. Future work will look at making generation faster and adding more ways for kids to play together. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
