AB  - This work presents design principles and promptengineering strategies for developing spatially aware Artificial Intelligence (AI) assistants in immersive environments. Focusing on the integration of AI and Virtual Reality (VR), we explore how multimodal, spatially grounded AI assistants can support humans in VR contexts. Drawing from literature in immersive Human-AI Interaction (HAX), we identify key requirements for egocentric, spatial, and contextual awareness. These insights informed the development of Novy, a Large Language Model (LLM)-based AI assistant prototype capable of spatial interactions in virtual environments through voice and gesture commands. Early evaluations indicate that Novy enhances high-level spatial interactions and user satisfaction, revealing design challenges and informing future work toward comprehensive design guidelines for spatially grounded and immersive AI assistants. © 2026 IEEE.
