AB  - Operator training in advanced manufacturing demands precise and specific feedback that scales beyond what human experts can provide. We present a Mixed Reality (MR) training system for thermoforming that integrates Large Language Model (LLM)-generated coaching directly into the operator’s practice workflow. Building on a validated physics-based heat transfer simulation and spatial performance dashboard from prior work, this paper introduces an Artificial Intelligence (AI)-based architecture that translates real-time simulation telemetry into structured, session-aware coaching delivered in-headset after each training run. Rather than generic feedback, each LLM coaching session is customized to the operator’s specific interaction patterns in each run and also is grounded in the process parameters such as zone-level temperature errors, energy consumption, and full prior-run history. This produces four labelled sections in the LLM coaching dashboard: Zone Analysis, Energy and Time, Trend, and an Overall Summary. A preliminary study with six novice operators found that all participants improved across four sequential training profiles, with group mean Zone Temperature Error reducing from 33.3 °C to 8.2 °C (a mean reduction of 74.9%). ‘LLM Coaching Specificity’ was the highest-rated category in the post study qualitative questionnaire (M = 6.42/7), where ‘Openness to AI’ and ‘Perceived Usefulness’ were also measured. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
