AB  - This paper presents an AI-driven immersive virtual reality (VR) learning framework that integrates agentic artificial intelligence, speech based interaction, and real-time multiplayer collaboration. The proposed system utilizes the Gemini large language model to generate adaptive questions and feedback within the VR environment. Gemini is employed through structured prompt engineering and contextual memory mechanisms rather than parameter-level fine-tuning, enabling domain adaptation without modifying model weights. A user study involving 25 participants was conducted to assess interaction flow, system responsibilities, and overall user experience. Multiplayer performance evaluation using Photon PUN indicated stable synchronization across concurrent sessions, with observed network delays remaining within acceptable bounds for real time interaction, as shown in Figure 3.2. Speech recognition errors, such as mispronunciations and partial utterances, were found to momentarily affect question flow. However, system-level recovery prompts and confidence based feedback mechanisms helped maintain feedback consistency. The core contributions of this work include the integration of AI orchestration within a VR learning environment, real time speech driven interaction, and an empirical multiplayer system analysis. Limitations of the study include a limited participant pool, reliance on cloud based AI services and sensitivity to network conditions © 2026 IEEE.
