AB  - This chapter explored the integration of virtual reality (VR) and generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) technologies as core components of the metaverse in filmmaking education, highlighting their potential to enhance accessibility, interactivity, and experiential learning. It begins with a comprehensive literature review covering the evolution of cinematography education, the integration of metaverse and VR technologies, the role of real-time rendering engines, and the emergence of artificial intelligence (AI)-driven feedback systems. The review examines how VR and AI can address the challenges of traditional film training by offering more accessible, cost-effective, and immersive learning environments. Building on this foundation, the chapter presents an empirical study that developed and evaluated a VR-based cinematography training platform equipped with an AI-powered assessment system. The study assessed the platform’s effectiveness in enhancing technical cinematographic skills such as lighting, framing, and camera placement. Results demonstrated a significant improvement in students’ self-reported knowledge and highlighted the benefits of immersive, iterative practice. However, several limitations were also identified, including interface complexity and issues related to the transparency of AI feedback. Overall, this chapter underscores the transformative potential of metaverse technologies in filmmaking education while emphasizing the need for ongoing system refinement to fully bridge virtual learning environments with real-world application. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Ali Darejeh and Samad Sepasgozar; individual chapters, the contributors.
