AB  - This paper proposes an original Text2VR-Art algorithm to achieve end-to-end dynamic construction of interactive 3D VR installation forms from text semantics, fundamentally addressing the shortcomings of existing solutions in real-time performance and semantic consistency. The algorithm adopts an end-to-end architecture comprising three core modules: a multi-semantic branch decoupling encoding module that uses an improved Transformer word embedding and a three-branch convolutional network to achieve accurate extraction and spatial alignment of form, style, and interactive semantics; a lightweight incremental dynamic 3D mesh generation module based on a pruning-optimized implicit field model and incremental update mechanism to meet the low-latency requirements of VR scenes; and a closed-loop feedback interactive semantic dynamic alignment module that ensures semantic consistency between interaction and form changes through semantic mapping of interactive behavior and adaptive fine-tuning of generation parameters. Experimental verification shows that the algorithm has a CD value of 0.087, an FID value of 11.32, an end-to-end latency of 12.6ms, a semantic matching accuracy of 94.6%, and a MOS score of 4.72. Its overall performance surpasses mainstream models such as NeRF and DreamFusion, as well as traditional VR solutions. It can meet the engineering application requirements of VR installation art interactive scenarios and provide technical support for the interdisciplinary research of computer graphics and digital art. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
